 "note": "BAC only, as before: Banpro's, Lafise's and Banco Avanz's card tariffs weren't reached in this pass. BAC Nicaragua's table of maximum credit card costs (in force from 1 October 2026), read in full: every personal card it lists (the business, fleet and PriceSmart Business cards aren't written, nor the Mastercard Local BAC, a córdoba card whose annual fee is priced in dollars), each in US dollars, the currency its fees are priced in, with its annual interest rate on dollar balances (20.04% on the Infinite, Signature, Black and Platinum cards, 24.00% on the Gold and Dorada cards, 30.00% on the Clásica and Standard cards), its annual fee for the holder (none where the table says Cortesía; waived for the first one or two years where it says so); a cash disbursement fee of 4%, at least 2 dollars; a minimum payment of at least 3.5% of the principal owed plus the period's interest; and the administrative charge for late payment, 1% of the principal in arrears, at most 15 dollars (10 for limits under 1,500 dollars, with a floor of 5, a band not written). The moratory rate is the ordinary rate plus up to half of it and isn't written as a penalty rate; the card brands' conversion fee abroad isn't stated as a figure. Wave 4 (30 October 2026) looked for more banks and added none: Banco Lafise Bancentro's tariff (read 30 October 2026) gives its cards' annual fees by credit limit but no interest rate, so its cards can't be written; Banpro's tariff page and Ficohsa Nicaragua's load their documents by script and give none to a plain request; BDF's site links no card terms; BAC's other pages didn't answer.",
